@startuml sequence-viewer-streaming
!include elvira.iuml
' What: with a `url` pdf.js loads the file in Range chunks; with a header callback the viewer fetches the chunks itself and refreshes an expired token once for all requests that hit 401 together, instead of breaking the read.
' Kind: UML sequence diagram. Scope: the viewer's document open (issue #151); the portal and catalog sides are the linked issues.
' Source: src/components/PDFViewer.vue, src/assets/utils/rangeTransport.ts, src/main.ts (2026-11-18)

title Streamed document open in EvilFlowersViewer (implemented on feature/151, not released, 2026-11-18)

participant "elvira-portal\n(host)" as host
participant "PDFViewer.vue" as viewer <<focus>>
participant "pdf.js worker" as pdfjs
participant "catalog\n(Range-capable)" as catalog

host -> viewer : renderViewer({ url, httpHeaders: fn, streaming })
activate viewer

alt httpHeaders is an object (fixed for the whole document)
  viewer -> pdfjs : getDocument({ url, httpHeaders, rangeChunkSize: 512 KiB })
  pdfjs -> catalog : GET url (read headers, then abort)
  pdfjs -> catalog : GET url, Range: bytes=a-b
  catalog --> pdfjs : 206 Partial Content
else httpHeaders is a function (refreshable)
  viewer -> host : httpHeaders({ retry: false })
  host --> viewer : { Authorization } (cached token)
  viewer -[$accent_msg()]> catalog : <b>GET url, Range: bytes=0-(chunk-1)</b>
  catalog --> viewer : 206 + Content-Range (total length)
  viewer -> pdfjs : getDocument({ range: RangeTransport(length, initialData) })
  loop each missing range (several in parallel)
    pdfjs -> viewer : requestDataRange(begin, end)
    viewer -> host : httpHeaders({ retry: false })
    viewer -> catalog : GET url, Range: bytes=begin-end
    alt 401 / 403 (token expired)
      catalog --> viewer : 401
      viewer -> host : httpHeaders({ retry: true }), one call shared by all concurrent 401s
      host --> viewer : { Authorization } (new token)
      viewer -> catalog : GET url, Range (retried once)
    end
    alt still failing
      viewer -> host : onStreamError({ status }), Reconnect notice
    else
      catalog --> viewer : 206 chunk
      viewer -> pdfjs : onDataRange(begin, chunk)
    end
  end
end

pdfjs --> viewer : PDFDocumentProxy
viewer -> host : onDocumentLoaded({ totalPages, source, streaming })
viewer -> pdfjs : getPage(initialPage).render()
viewer -> host : onFirstPageRendered({ page, durationMs, source, streaming, bytesLoaded })
viewer -> host : onLoadProgress({ loaded, total }) (background fetch, unless streaming)
deactivate viewer

caption With `streaming: true` pdf.js fetches only the ranges the open page needs (disableAutoFetch + disableStream). Otherwise it keeps fetching in the background, so search and print behave as with `data`.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersViewer · docs/diagrams/sequence-viewer-streaming.puml
@enduml
